    <string name="prop_solar_body2">Current: SFI %1$d, K %2$s (%3$s). Saved NOAA outlook covers %4$d more days.\n\nThese numbers matter less than you might think: on real reception data, month-old values cost under 1%% accuracy. Off-grid, the app uses the saved outlook, then the value from 27 days earlier. You can enter numbers heard on WWV (18 min past the hour) or a net, or share yours with the net as a #SWX line.</string>
